        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Indonesia begins enforcing social media ban for children under-16s Asia / Pacific Issued on: 28/03/2026 - 12:35 Indonesia began enforcing a social media ban for children under the age of 16 on Saturday, after a minister warned digital platforms there was \"no room for compromise.\" he Southeast Asian nation announced the ban this month citing threats from online pornography, cyberbullying and internet addiction, as concerns grow globally over the impact of social media on children's wellbeing. North Korea's Kim Jong Un gifted gun by Belarusian leader 27/03/2026 Europe India's historic haveli homes caught between revival and ruin 25/03/2026 Asia / Pacific EU and Australia sign free trade deal and boost defence cooperation 24/03/2026 Europe EU signs trade deal with Australia as it looks for new partners amid tension with US 24/03/2026 Europe Mumbai celebrates local new year 19/03/2026 Asia / Pacific Kyrgyzstan: White yak breeders hope for recognition amid agricultural revival 17/03/2026 Asia / Pacific Sri Lanka and Thailand bring in fuel-rationing measures amidst Middle East war 16/03/2026 Asia / Pacific Why North Korea just fired rockets during US-South Korea military drills 15/03/2026 Asia / Pacific Six members of Iranian women's football team granted asylum in Australia 11/03/2026 Middle East"
